these women  are part of the million strong health  activists better known as asha workers  combing india's villages in the hunt for  coronavirus  identifiable in their bright outfits  each frontline worker  is in charge of more than a thousand  people  they check screen monitor  track and advice  to keep the country's rural population  healthy and pandemic free  but it's not just the virus they are  exposed to  they are seen as government informers  and are abused and beaten  this asha worker who doesn't want to be  identified was attacked  while tracking a covid19 patient in her  village  then they hit my daughter on the head  with an iron rod she is still suffering  [Music]  entrusted with dozens of assignments  including a check on maternal mortality  malnourishment vaccination and family  planning  their work now is almost entirely  consumed by the pandemic  and with limited training  as volunteers their own health is at  risk with barely any protection  they are on call day and night for a  monthly salary  of just 50 pounds  we risk both ours and our children's  lives whenever we get back from the  field  some of us have small children who want  to hug us as soon as we get home  before we have the chance to bathe or  even wash our hands  many have been infected on the job and  dozens have succumbed to the virus  ignored mistreated and overworked they  now protest across the country for  better pay and protection  19 has spread to almost every corner of  the country  the poor are most vulnerable  and now more than ever the nation needs  this army of frontline  workers neville lazarus sky news  sony park
 

